cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released per-segment predictions, please cite the paper below."
title: "Participant identity, not anxiety: segment-level partitioning inflates EEG affect classification on the DASPS dataset"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Javed
    given-names: Abdullah
    affiliation: "Changchun University of Science and Technology"
  - family-names: Guo
    given-names: Bin
    affiliation: "Changchun University of Science and Technology"
  - family-names: Miantezila Junior
    given-names: Milembolo
    affiliation: "Changchun University of Science and Technology"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/USERNAME/dasps-participant-confound"
abstract: >-
  Code, per-segment predictions and analysis scripts showing that segment-level
  cross-validation on the DASPS EEG dataset measures participant identity
  rather than anxiety, because a single HAM-A score per participant is
  inherited by all 180 of that participant's one-second segments.
keywords:
  - EEG
  - anxiety recognition
  - DASPS
  - data leakage
  - participant-independent evaluation
  - reproducibility
